course: dictionary
lesson: 6640
title: Abbreviations and game words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer phrase. NPC is short for "non-player character", so each letter stands for a word. You will see it written as NPC, or as NPCs when there is more than one.
explain: In a game, the player is the person holding the controller. A non-player character is anyone else who is run by the computer, such as a shopkeeper, a villager or a guard. «NPC means "non-player character", a game character controlled by the computer; NPCs follow code and don't understand or care.»
explain: Some words change meaning depending on who is using them. NPC is also slang, and some people use it as a rude insult for someone who seems dull, follows the crowd or does not think for themselves. That use is unkind, so never call a real person an NPC. Use the context to tell which meaning is meant: is the sentence about a game, or about a person?
fact: NPC is an abbreviation: it stands for non-player character.
fact: NPCs is the plural, meaning more than one non-player character.
fact: «NPC» means a character in a video game controlled by the computer, not by a player.
fact: Gamers often say phrases like «talk to the NPC» and «NPC behaviour».
fact: As slang, «NPC» is a rude insult, so it is unkind to use it about a real person.
exercise: What does the abbreviation NPC stand for? | *Non-player character | Nice, polite character | Night path check | New player controller
exercise: In a game, a shopkeeper who says the same line again and again is most likely what? | A save file | The player | A map | *An NPC
exercise: «NPCs follow code and don't understand or care.» What does this tell you about NPCs? | *They are controlled by the computer and do not really think | They can write their own code | They are players who choose their own moves | They are always kind to the player
test: In «talk to the NPC», what kind of thing is the NPC? | A type of game console | *A game character controlled by the computer | A real teacher in a classroom | A player's friend on the phone
test: Why should you not call a classmate an NPC? | Because it is the name of a game | *Because it is a rude, unkind insult | Because it means they are very clever | Because it is a long word
exam: Which sentence uses NPC with its game meaning? | You are such an NPC, just copy everyone | My NPC homework is due today | The NPC in our class always follows the crowd | *Talk to the NPC by the castle gate to get the map
